  ;; Imaging WITHOUT `java.desktop`: decode/encode, transforms, vector drawing,
  ;; text, SVG rasterisation and plotting, in-process over a first-party Rust
  ;; cdylib (image + resvg/tiny-skia) through the JDK Foreign Function & Memory
  ;; API. This is what replaced AWT/Java2D/ImageIO/jsvg everywhere in vis — no
  ;; vis code touches `java.awt`/`javax.imageio` any more, so there is no
  ;; headless bootstrap, no fontconfig, and SVG rasterisation finally works in
  ;; the macOS binary. Fonts are embedded in the cdylib (four Noto faces).
  ;; `java.desktop` itself is still loaded, and that is FINE: mic capture uses
  ;; `javax.sound.sampled` (the JDK's only microphone API), and two third-party,
  ;; non-graphical users pull it too — Apache POI (value classes in xlsx/pptx
  ;; writing) and next.jdbc's `clojure.java.data` (`java.beans.Introspector`).
  com.blockether/imaging {:mvn/version "0.1.4"}
